---
import Marketing from '@layouts/Marketing.astro';

// Raw markup, lifted verbatim from the page this replaces.
const body = `<div class="wrap">
  <section class="band doc" style="border-top:none">
<h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
<p class="meta">Effective: 2026-08-27 · Contact: see <a href="/support">Support</a></p>
<p class="txt">Moshpit is a terminal. Your data is none of our business, and the app is
built so it never becomes our business.</p>

<h3>What we collect</h3>
<p class="txt"><strong>Nothing.</strong> Moshpit has no analytics, no crash-reporting
service, no advertising SDKs, no tracking, and no accounts. The one server we
operate is a push relay for agent notifications, and it is built so it cannot
read what it carries — see <em>Notifications</em> below.</p>

<h3>Where your data lives</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Connection details</strong> (hosts, usernames, ports) are stored on
your device.</li>
<li><strong>Passwords and private keys</strong> are stored in the iOS Keychain,
protected by the Secure Enclave where available. They never leave your device
except as part of the SSH/Mosh handshake with the server <em>you</em> configured.</li>
<li><strong>Terminal content</strong> exists only in transit between your device
and your servers, encrypted by SSH or Mosh (AES-128-OCB3), and on your screen.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Network connections</h3>
<p class="txt">Terminal traffic goes exclusively to servers you add. Beyond that, the app
talks to exactly one endpoint of ours — the push relay, and only to register or
renew notification pairings: no telemetry, no update pings, no font or CDN
fetches. The Local Network permission is requested only so SSH/Mosh can reach
hosts on your own LAN (e.g. 192.168.x.x); iOS would otherwise silently drop
that traffic.</p>

<h3>Notifications &amp; Live Activities</h3>
<p class="txt">The Dynamic Island Live Activity and in-app alerts are generated
<em>on your device</em> from your own session data.</p>
<p class="txt">Remote notifications — the alerts that reach you when the app is closed —
are sealed <em>on your own host</em> with a per-host key that only your device
holds. They travel through Moshpit's push relay and Apple's push service as
ciphertext: neither can read the agent's name, the command, or anything else
inside; the text is decrypted by a notification extension on your device. To
deliver at all, the relay necessarily handles your device's Apple push token
and sees when a paired host sends; it stores no message content. What the Live
Activity shows on the lock screen can be limited with <em>Show detail on lock
screen</em> in Settings, and pushed notifications additionally respect iOS's
own <em>Show Previews</em> setting.</p>

<h3>Purchases</h3>
<p class="txt">Moshpit is a one-time purchase handled entirely by Apple's App Store. We
receive no payment information.</p>

<h3>Changes</h3>
<p class="txt">If this policy ever changes, the new version ships with an app update and is
dated at the top. Since the app collects nothing, the realistic change is
wording, not substance.</p>

<hr>

<h3>隐私政策</h3>
<p class="txt">Moshpit 是一个终端。<strong>我们不收集任何数据</strong>：无分析、无崩溃上报服务、
无广告 SDK、无跟踪、无账号。我们运营的唯一服务是一个通知推送中转，它读不了自己承载的内容（见下）。</p>
<ul>
<li>连接信息存于你的设备；密码与私钥存于 iOS 钥匙串（有 Secure Enclave 则由其保护），
除与你自己配置的服务器做 SSH/Mosh 握手外绝不离开设备。</li>
<li>终端内容只在你的设备与你的服务器之间加密传输（SSH / Mosh AES-128-OCB3）。</li>
<li>终端流量只去你添加的服务器；本地网络权限仅用于访问局域网主机。</li>
<li>灵动岛与 App 内提醒在设备本地生成。App 关闭时的远程通知，在你自己的主机上、
用只有你设备持有的密钥密封，经 Moshpit 推送中转与 Apple 以密文送达——两者都读不到内容，
解密发生在你设备上的通知扩展里。为完成投递，中转需要处理你设备的 Apple 推送令牌、
能看到配对主机何时发送；它不存储任何消息内容。</li>
<li>购买由 Apple App Store 处理，我们接触不到任何支付信息。</li>
</ul>
  </section>
</div>`;
---

<Marketing
  title="Privacy Policy — Moshpit"
  description="Moshpit collects nothing. No analytics, no crash reporting, no accounts — and a push relay that cannot read what it carries."
  path="privacy"
  lang="en"
  translated={false}
>
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
</Marketing>
